# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 11 of the Tutorial

[A low-pass RC (the Bode plot)]

e,1,0,1
r1,1,2,1000
c1,2,0,1e-6

analysis: ac
note: In this problem, we draw a Bode plot for the first time: plot v_2 between 10 and 100000 Hz and see the low-pass rolloff — flat, then falling 20 dB per decade with the phase heading for -90°. The Plot card re-solves the circuit at every frequency, which is why it takes the circuit and an answer's name rather than an expression.
omega: 1
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
plottool: bode
plotkey: v_2
plotmin: 10
plotmax: 100000
plotpoints: 300


[AS7's Example 14.7 (series resonance)]

e,1,0,20
r,1,2,2
l,2,3,1'm
c,3,0,.4'u

analysis: ac
note: Find the resonance frequency of the series RLC — solve im(ze) = 0 with w > 0 and real solutions only: 50000 rad/s. For the bandwidth frequencies, solve abs(ze) = sqrt(2)*2 with w<50000 and then w>50000: 49010 and 51010 rad/s.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1407.png [447px]
omega: w
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(ze) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes
plottool: bode
plotkey: i_l
plotmin: 100
plotmax: 100000
plotpoints: 300


[AS7's Example 14.8 (parallel resonance)]

e,1,0,10
r,1,0,8'k
l,1,0,.2'm
c,1,0,8'u

analysis: ac
note: Find the resonance frequency of the parallel RLC: 25000 rad/s. The chapter uses im(ie) rather than im(ze) here because the calculator's numerical search could not find so sharp a peak. Version 9 solves symbolically and would manage either, but the equation says something true: at resonance the source's current is in phase with its voltage.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1408.png [498px]
omega: w
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(ie) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes
plottool: bode
plotkey: i_l
plotmin: 10
plotmax: 100000
plotpoints: 300


[AS7's Example 14.9 (resonance from a node voltage)]

j,0,1,1
c,1,0,.1
r1,1,0,10
l,1,2,2
r2,2,0,2

analysis: ac
note: Determine the resonant frequency of the circuit: solve im(v1) = 0 with w > 0 and real solutions only, which gives 2 rad/s.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1409.png [504px]
omega: w
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no
solve_equations: im(v1) = 0
solve_unknowns: w
solve_conditions: w>0
solve_real_only: yes
plottool: bode
plotkey: i_l
plotmin: 0.01
plotmax: 10
plotpoints: 300
